{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"The differential equation is separable.\n\nWhat does it look like after we separate the variables?","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"$dy=\\left(3t^2+1\\right) dt$\n\nLet's integrate both sides of the equation.\n\n$\\displaystyle\\int dy=\\int\\left(3t^2+1\\right) dt$\n\nWhat do we get?","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"$y=t^3+t+C$\n\nWhat value of $C$ satisfies the initial condition $y(1)=5$?","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"Let's substitute $t=1$ and $y=5$ into the equation and solve for $C$.\n\n$\\begin{align}\n5\u0026=1^3+1+C\\\\\n\\\\\nC\u0026=3\n\\end{align}$\n\nNow use this value of $C$ to find $t$ when $y=3$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"$\\begin{align}\n3\u0026=t^3+t+3\\\\\n\\\\\n0\u0026=t^3+t\\\\\n\\\\\n0\u0026=\\red{\\cancel{(t^2+1)}}\\cdot t\\\\\n\\\\\nt\u0026=0\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"$\\dfrac{dy}{dt}=3t^2+1$ and $y(1)=5$.\n\n**What is $t$ when $y=3$?**\n\n[[☃ radio 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"radio 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"choices":[{"content":"$t=-\\dfrac32$","correct":false},{"content":"$t=-1$","correct":false},{"content":"$t=0$","correct":true},{"content":"$t=1$","correct":false},{"content":"$t=\\dfrac32$","correct":false}],"deselectEnabled":false,"displayCount":null,"hasNoneOfTheAbove":false,"multipleSelect":false,"onePerLine":true,"randomize":true},"static":false,"type":"radio","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
